--- a/docs/R22-E2LB-FIX-REVIEW.md
+++ b/docs/R22-E2LB-FIX-REVIEW.md
@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+# R22 — E2LB handshake / iAP2 parser and media hardening (EXPERIMENTAL)
+
+Date: 2026-11-22. Base: the exact 683-file `mcarplay-R21-E2LB-adversarial-source-EXPERIMENTAL.zip` previously delivered. This is a source correction, **not** a confirmed vehicle fix or installable APK.
+
+## Corrected
+
+1. **Deterministic iAP2 payload-checksum bug** (`iap2/Iap2LinkEngine.kt`): `receive.take(length)` already consumes a broken frame; removed an additional `receive.discard(1)` which previously consumed the next frame's first `FF` byte. Added regression tests for a broken packet followed by a good packet and a fragmented `FF 55 ...` marker preceding a good packet. Markers, invalid headers, bad payloads, invalid lengths and unframed bytes now have distinct payload-free counters. `Iap2LinkChannel` emits a `LINK-PARSER` summary on termination.
+2. **Truthful E2LB greeting log**: after optional `0x4E0D` is skipped, the summary no longer falsely reports it as sent.
+3. **Opt-in E2LB-only `0x4300` shape experiment**: added two-group encoding with a wired identifier `00008110 + MAC (uppercase, compact) + 0000` and the lowercase wireless MAC in group 1. The current single-group encoding remains the default. A **Display settings → E2LB 双标识 CarPlay 实验** switch can enable it on the *next* connection. The switch is ignored for other receiver models and for an unknown/placeholder Bluetooth identity. This experiment is not evidence that the head unit will send `0x4301`.
+4. **ABR codec update no longer holds network write lock** (`video/VideoSender.kt`). Codec bitrate updates run after frame write/synchronization finishes, under a separate lock also held while releasing the codec, with stale codec/state checks. Hardware `setParameters` must succeed before the ABR model commits; a rejected or stale decision cannot update the model.
+5. **Transcoder input-drop statistics** (`video/CarWithTranscoder.kt`): count all decoder-input loss paths (`NO_BUFFER`, `NULL_BUFFER`, `OVERSIZE`, `CODEC_ERROR`) once each, with totals and reason counts. Previously only the busy/no-buffer branch incremented the counter.
+6. **IDR recovery state reset**: added an explicit `IdrResync.reset()` for new source generations. When source dimensions change, the request throttle resets but the pipeline still waits for a fresh IDR; stale P frames are not admitted.
+
+## Deliberately not changed
+
+- `0x4E0A` language `zh-CN`, greeting ordering and entire-carplay profile inference: no receiver-side evidence yet supports a global change.
+- Always-on `MulticastLock`: R21 already scopes modern NSD publish and discovery to the car Wi-Fi `Network`; modern Android NSD does not universally require a multicast lock. Android 17 vehicle and network-change checks remain outstanding.
+- `AirPlayCrypto.chachaOpen`: the earlier report verified that bad authentication tags were not silently swallowed in R21. No redundant rewrite.
+- `0x4300` dual-group is not forced on by default. Other known tests with E2LB have not proven it solves this receiver-side silence.
+- The application still cannot read the true local Bluetooth MAC on every unprivileged Android build; the current limitation cannot be bypassed by simply granting `BLUETOOTH_CONNECT`.
+
+## Tests actually executed here
+
+- 23 Kotlin/JVM test methods: iAP2 link negotiation/ACK/duplication and checksum recovery, E2LB dual-group payload policy, ABR model state and rejection handling. **23 PASS / 0 FAIL**, compiled and run with the locally available Kotlin 1.9 CLI and minimal JUnit API shims (not the Android Gradle test runner).
+- Additional actual Kotlin parser/protocol smoke runner: 15 PASS / 0 FAIL; Kotlin 1.9 compatibility adapter is only for existing Kotlin-2 `ArrayDeque.addLast` in the isolated smoke compilation, **production source untouched**.
+- Python tool suite: **87 PASS / 0 FAIL**.
+- Android XML resources/layout: both parse.
+- R21 baseline compared byte-for-byte against original R21 ZIP: all 683 original files matched before modifications.
+
+### Unavailable/blocked verification
+
+- `./gradlew --offline --no-daemon :app:testStandardDebugUnitTest` cannot start: local Gradle 8.10.2 distribution absent and wrapper fails DNS resolution at `services.gradle.org`. Android SDK, Android lint and APK compilation were not run here. **Do not assume this source builds cleanly on Android until CI is run.**
+- E2LB parking-condition vehicle validation has not been run. The observed 2026-11-22 failure was already upstream of screen/audio. It remains necessary to capture receiver `0x4301`, `_carplay-ctrl` invite, AirPlay discovery and `SETUP 200`, and then verify picture/sound/touch.
+
+## A/B validation in parked vehicle
+
+1. Install a CI-verified test APK from this source only after checking package/signing; enable the same car Wi-Fi and Bluetooth. Leave E2LB dual-group switch **off** in first attempt. Export redacted log.
+2. Enable `E2LB 双标识 CarPlay 实验` under Display settings, reconnect and export another log.
+3. Compare `iap2 0x4300 形态=...`, `LINK-PARSER`, `0x4301`, ctrl invite count, `_airplay._tcp` discovery, SETUP status. A `pair-verify 200` without `SETUP 200` is not full CarPlay activation. Do not force repeated SETUP to guessed gateway:7000.
+4. If dual-group doesn't help, turn the switch **off** and keep the source's R20/R21 fallback intact.
+
+The repository's previous R20/R21 ZIPs and APKs were not overwritten; changes exist only in this R22 source copy.
